From b9b3e66eae535f36c5e39449f582bf969b4a9294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:26:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] yblod-engine-vk: DVVK_PACK_ONE_ROW=1 (pack: one output
 row per invocation)

S_ROWS (constant 28) = 1: the regular pack variants (not the Annex B or GUI
tiles, which assume two rows) write a 4 x 1 block per invocation instead of
4 x 2; each block fetches its chroma rows itself. Fewer pixels in flight:
the bilinear fused pack 61 -> 54 registers (V3D), but the staged Annex B
pack 33 -> 42; neither reaches 4 threads, so it is a switch for the Pi's
measurement, off by default. The engine sizes the dispatch by the variant
in use. Outputs identical.
---
